      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "The model behind [Ramsey Steady State Explorer](note:ramsey-steady-state-explorer). Place the view, not this note."
      },
      {
       "t": "prose",
       "md": "- **Model.** The steady state of the [Ramsey-Cass-Koopmans Model](note:ramsey-cass-koopmans-model) with $f(k) = Ak^{\\alpha}$: $f'(\\bar{k}) = 1/\\beta - 1 + \\delta$, $\\bar{c} = f(\\bar{k}) - \\delta\\bar{k}$, $s = \\delta\\bar{k}/f(\\bar{k})$. The [Golden Rule Saving Rate](note:golden-rule-saving-rate) benchmark has $f'(k^{*}) = \\delta$.\n- **Tests.** Closed-form values computed in Python: the lecture's practice economy at $\\beta = 0.95$ ($\\bar{k} = 10.73$, $s = 0.328$), $\\beta = 0.90$ and $0.99$, and the $\\alpha = 1/3$, $\\delta = 0.05$ case."
      }
     ],
